      "content": "hey i'm working on some calculations regarding the lunar density and the orbital mechanics, and nothing is adding up. when i run the mass-to-volume ratio based on the standard gravitational constant, the density values are coming out way too low for a solid rock core. it's like the mass is being distributed in a shell rather than a sphere. i think i'm missing a variable for the internal void/hollow structure. can you help me look at the math to see how much void space would be needed to make this density figure work?",
